1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,071
Tens of thousands of chemicals are in commerce.

2
00:00:03,351 --> 00:00:08,191
A few hundred have been tested for their effect on the developing nervous system.

3
00:00:08,711 --> 00:00:19,553
The modern alternative to an animal study is to grow cortical neurons on a microelectrode
array, and watch whether they organise themselves into a firing network.

4
00:00:19,833 --> 00:00:21,086
It is faster.

5
00:00:21,366 --> 00:00:25,161
It still costs days of culture, for every single compound.

6
00:00:25,681 --> 00:00:29,740
So the binding question is not "is this chemical neurotoxic".

7
00:00:30,020 --> 00:00:30,823
It is:

8
00:00:30,943 --> 00:00:32,971
which ones go on the plate first?

9
00:00:33,801 --> 00:00:35,080
First, the trap.

10
00:00:35,360 --> 00:00:41,100
A chemical that simply kills the culture flattens every electrical measurement you can make.

11
00:00:41,380 --> 00:00:45,355
Calling that neuroactive is how this kind of screen fools itself.

12
00:00:45,875 --> 00:00:49,287
So the outcome is defined against viability.

13
00:00:49,567 --> 00:00:56,498
A network effect counts only when it happens at least three-fold below the concentration
that kills the cells.

14
00:00:56,778 --> 00:00:59,040
Forty-nine compounds qualify.

15
00:00:59,320 --> 00:01:03,794
Twenty-eight are inconclusive, and we publish them as inconclusive.

16
00:01:04,624 --> 00:01:06,140
From a structure alone:

17
00:01:06,260 --> 00:01:14,777
standardise it, fingerprint it, and find its nearest measured relatives among a hundred and
two chemicals whose answer we already know.

18
00:01:15,297 --> 00:01:19,705
Their outcomes, weighted by chemical similarity, become a score.

19
00:01:19,985 --> 00:01:24,767
A conformal prediction set turns that score into a statement of confidence.

20
00:01:25,047 --> 00:01:29,908
And when the nearest relative is too distant to say anything, the tool says nothing.

21
00:01:30,738 --> 00:01:37,544
Test in the order the model recommends, and half the active compounds appear after
thirty-two assays.

22
00:01:37,824 --> 00:01:40,787
In a random order, fifty-one and a half.

23
00:01:41,067 --> 00:01:45,428
Across two hundred independent splits, thirty-three to thirty-four.

24
00:01:45,948 --> 00:01:47,650
Area under the curve:

25
00:01:47,770 --> 00:01:55,359
zero point eight two eight on the pre-declared split, zero point seven seven six as the
median of twenty others.

26
00:01:55,879 --> 00:02:02,391
This is a retrospective evaluation, on a cohort the agency deliberately enriched with
suspects.

27
00:02:03,221 --> 00:02:04,351
We attacked it.

28
00:02:04,631 --> 00:02:06,332
Then somebody else did.

29
00:02:06,852 --> 00:02:15,110
A separate agent, which never saw our code, rebuilt the labels from the agency spreadsheet,
and reimplemented the method from scratch.

30
00:02:15,389 --> 00:02:16,335
Agreement:

31
00:02:16,455 --> 00:02:19,319
five parts in ten to the seventeenth.

32
00:02:19,839 --> 00:02:28,197
Then it shuffled the labels between chemical scaffolds, nine hundred and ninety-nine times,
refitting everything on every shuffle.

33
00:02:28,717 --> 00:02:31,293
Not one shuffle reached our result.

34
00:02:31,573 --> 00:02:34,611
p equals zero point zero zero one.

35
00:02:35,441 --> 00:02:38,857
The decision itself runs inside SciencePal.

36
00:02:39,137 --> 00:02:47,138
The agent receives the measured analogues, twenty chemicals withheld from everything, and
our scoring code — and not our answer.

37
00:02:47,658 --> 00:02:50,164
Its chemical database was blocked.

38
00:02:50,444 --> 00:02:56,116
It said so, found another route, and recovered a compound our own pipeline had thrown away:

39
00:02:56,236 --> 00:02:59,697
the only one of the twenty it could call with confidence.

40
00:03:00,527 --> 00:03:03,209
This does not tell you a chemical is safe.

41
00:03:03,489 --> 00:03:08,000
A negative result in a dish does not exclude harm in development.

42
00:03:08,520 --> 00:03:11,168
It tells you which plate to run on Monday.

43
00:03:11,448 --> 00:03:13,910
The five it chose are a prediction.

44
00:03:14,190 --> 00:03:16,408
One experiment would settle them.
